<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_Process_LeanDocsPublish" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_LeanDocsPublish">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_LeanDocsPublish" name="Publish a folio's Lean render with the harness chrome" processRef="Process_LeanDocsPublish"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_LeanDocsPublish" name="Publish a folio's Lean render with the harness chrome" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Build the visualiser of a folio's declared `lean` directory — the Lake package's doc-gen4 HTML render — and put it inside the folio's built site with the harness navbar and rail.

Two steps in two lanes. The build is a Lake run over the folio's warm olean cache: expensive, and able to damage the cache (a Lake build over an untraced restore evicts it), so it sits with the Lean toolchain and refuses rather than risks. The publish is a file pass over the build's output that cannot touch the cache; it sits with the build pipeline, after the site is built and before the chrome check and deploy, where `stage-folio-local.ts` rails the folio's own pages.

Only End_Ready publishes: a refused guard, a failed build and an unrailed page are each reported as such, never as a complete site without Lean docs.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <!-- STRICT: the publish step's own last act is an assertion that every
           staged page is railed or declined, and a partial render must not
           reach the deploy as though it were whole. -->
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_LeanDocsPublish">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Lean" name="Lean toolchain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns the Lake run. Hands GW_Built a render directory or a refusal; it never publishes, so nothing it does reaches a reader until Lane_Build has railed and checked it.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="lean-toolchain"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Changed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Build</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Built</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_NoRender</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Build" name="CI/CD Pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns the site. Takes the render from Task_Build, rails it with the platform's own pass, and either hands it on to the folio's chrome check and deploy or stops it at End_Unrailed.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="build-pipeline"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Publish</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Railed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Ready</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Unrailed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Changed" name="The folio's Lean sources&#10;or its site changed">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Build" name="Build the doc-gen4 render&#10;over the warm cache">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `lean-html-docs` (`adapters/paper/lean/lean-docs-build.sh --lake-root &lt;pkg&gt; --lib &lt;Lib&gt;`). Refuses while another lake/lean process holds `.lake/`, refuses over a restored tree with no traces, checks or restores the warm cache, enables the sentinel-commented doc-gen4 require for this build only, then `lake -R -Kenv=dev build &lt;Lib&gt;:docs`. Output: `&lt;pkg&gt;/.lake/build/doc`.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="lean-html-docs"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Built" name="Is there a&#10;render?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by Task_Build's exit code: 0 and a render directory, or a refusal (2: a guard; 3: no warm cache) or a failed build (1). Only 0 continues.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_NoRender" name="No render — refused&#10;or failed; nothing published">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Publish" name="Stage the render under the&#10;site and rail every page">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `lean-render-publish` (`adapters/paper/lean/lean-render.ts --docs &lt;render&gt; --site &lt;site&gt;`). Copies the render to `&lt;site&gt;/lean/` without Lake's bookkeeping, marks doc-gen4's iframe navbar and `find/` redirect rail-declined, adds the layout shim, optionally prunes to the folio's modules, then runs `rail-standalone-pages.ts --foreign-site` over the whole site and checks every staged page.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="lean-html-docs"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Railed" name="Every page railed&#10;or declined?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by Task_Publish's own closing assertion: a staged page carrying neither the harness rail nor the `folio-navbar: none` opt-out fails it (exit 1).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Ready" name="Lean pages ready for the&#10;chrome check and deploy">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Unrailed" name="Pages without chrome —&#10;not published">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0" sourceRef="Start_Changed" targetRef="Task_Build"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Task_Build" targetRef="GW_Built"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="GW_Built" targetRef="Task_Publish" name="yes — built"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="GW_Built" targetRef="End_NoRender" name="no"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="Task_Publish" targetRef="GW_Railed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="GW_Railed" targetRef="End_Ready" name="yes"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="GW_Railed" targetRef="End_Unrailed" name="no"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_LeanDocsPublish">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_LeanDocsPublish" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_LeanDocsPublish">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_LeanDocsPublish" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_LeanDocsPublish" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="60" width="1140" height="480" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Lean" bpmnElement="Lane_Lean" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="90" y="60" width="1110" height="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Build" bpmnElement="Lane_Build" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="90" y="300" width="1110" height="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Changed" bpmnElement="Start_Changed">
        <dc:Bounds x="122" y="92" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="162" y="132" width="90" height="126" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Build" bpmnElement="Task_Build">
        <dc:Bounds x="270" y="72" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Built" bpmnElement="GW_Built" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="505" y="85" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="559" y="139" width="90" height="35" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_NoRender" bpmnElement="End_NoRender">
        <dc:Bounds x="702" y="92" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Publish" bpmnElement="Task_Publish">
        <dc:Bounds x="470" y="320" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Railed" bpmnElement="GW_Railed" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="705" y="355" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="759" y="409" width="90" height="53" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Ready" bpmnElement="End_Ready">
        <dc:Bounds x="902" y="362" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Unrailed" bpmnElement="End_Unrailed">
        <dc:Bounds x="712" y="472" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="618" y="454" width="90" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_0" bpmnElement="Flow_0">
        <di:waypoint x="158" y="110" />
        <di:waypoint x="214" y="110" />
        <di:waypoint x="214" y="132" />
        <di:waypoint x="270" y="132" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_1" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <di:waypoint x="390" y="132" />
        <di:waypoint x="447.5" y="132" />
        <di:waypoint x="447.5" y="110" />
        <di:waypoint x="505" y="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_2" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <di:waypoint x="530" y="135" />
        <di:waypoint x="530" y="340" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="534" y="228.5" width="90" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_3" bpmnElement="Flow_3">
        <di:waypoint x="555" y="110"/>
        <di:waypoint x="702" y="110"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_4" bpmnElement="Flow_4">
        <di:waypoint x="590" y="380" />
        <di:waypoint x="705" y="380" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_5" bpmnElement="Flow_5">
        <di:waypoint x="755" y="380"/>
        <di:waypoint x="902" y="380"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_6" bpmnElement="Flow_6">
        <di:waypoint x="730" y="405"/>
        <di:waypoint x="730" y="472"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
